		-- ── THE PROFILE PHRASE on the front of the card (Easy Chat) ─────────────────────────────────
		-- Ola's own card reads "I am TRAINER! I'm pleased to meet you.", which is what made this
		-- provable rather than plausible: it is template bank 94 entry 1, "I am {0}! I'm pleased to meet
		-- you.", with the word TRAINER in the slot. Everything below is the game's own algorithm, read
		-- out of ARM9 rather than inferred:
		--   the TEMPLATE is group u16(card+0x6C) into the bank table at 0x0209F73C =
		--   [94,96,99,93,98,95,97], entry u16(card+0x6E). Counts 20/20/20/20/20/21/2, so ECT is those
		--   123 templates flat and the index is groupStart + entry.
		--   a WORD is FUN_02024854 -> FUN_020248F4: `id &= 0x7FF`, then walk the 13 category sizes at
		--   0x0209F7AA cumulatively and take `id - cumulativeStart` from that category's bank
		--   (table at 0x0209F7C4). 0xFFFF is the game's own "no word" sentinel.
		-- ⭐ ECW IS THOSE 13 CATEGORIES CONCATENATED IN THE GAME'S OWN ORDER, so the flat id indexes it
		-- directly and the cumulative walk collapses to one bounds check — the same answer the game's
		-- loop gives, without reimplementing the loop. Every category size was verified against the real
		-- entry count of its bank at bake time, which is what makes that equivalence safe.
