	-- Transitions list doesn't read "Nuvema Town" for a door — distinct from real area connectors (routes). gen:
	-- research/re/gen_house_zones.py. Rule (RE 2026-06-29): borrows its parent area's place-name (zonedata +0x1a
	-- idx == parent's) AND indoor (zonedata +0x1c camera-bound field == 0) AND not bannered (disp bit == 0) AND
	-- its parent area IS a town/city or route on the game's own town map (a/0/8/6 row field 0x0B <= 1).
	-- ⛔ THAT LAST TEST IS THE 2026-08-24 CORRECTION, and the header it replaces was confidently wrong: it
	-- claimed the rule "EXCLUDES bannered places (Relic Castle/Desert Resort)", which was only ever true of a
	-- dungeon's HEAD zone. Its inner rooms are disp 0, indoor, and share the dungeon's name, so all of them
	-- passed — 49 DUNGEON INTERIORS sat on this list, and every stairway inside Relic Castle (29 chambers) and
	-- Dragonspiral Tower (8 floors) announced itself as "house", along with Cold Storage's containers,
	-- Celestial Tower, Abundant Shrine, Lostlorn Forest, P2 Laboratory, Liberty Garden, Twist Mountain,
	-- Dreamyard and Unity Tower. Found from Ola's report that "the actual cold storage is just a house on the
	-- nav list"; they now fall through to the game's own place name, which is Ola's answer (2026-08-24: leave
	-- the game's own naming alone, and no invented word to tell inside from outside).
	-- ⛔⛔ AND IT WAS STILL HALF WRONG UNTIL 2026-08-31 (Ola, in N's Castle: "all the transitions inside there
	-- speak house, even though the map name doesn't change"). The test was written NEGATIVELY — "the parent
	-- area must not be a LANDMARK", `mtype.get(area, 0) >= 2` — so an area with NO town-map row at all fell
	-- through that DEFAULT of 0 and counted as a town. N's Castle's parent area is zone 264, the castle
	-- itself, which has no row in either ROM because you cannot fly there, so all fourteen interiors 265-278
	-- passed and every door and stairway inside the castle announced "house". ABSENCE IS NOT EVIDENCE OF
	-- BEING A TOWN: the test is now POSITIVE (present, and type 0 town/city or 1 route). Measured over all
	-- 427 zones (research/re/house_rule_check.py): 21 zones leave the list and NONE join it — N's Castle's
	-- fourteen, the Union Room 422 with its battle rooms 150/151 (entered from a Wi-Fi menu, never a field
	-- warp, so nothing in the nav list changes), and Black City's 2/3/4/5, which the union below puts back.
	-- ⚠ TWO ROMS, ONE TABLE. a/0/8/6 is VERSION-EXCLUSIVE — White lists White Forest (area 424, type 0) and
	-- no Black City; Black lists Black City (area 0, type 0) and no White Forest — while the zonedata a/0/1/2
	-- is byte-identical between the ROMs. Both measured this session, not assumed. So the generator reads
	-- BOTH ROMs and unions the result: a house in EITHER game stays a house in this one shared table.
	-- ⚠ ONE CURATED EXCEPTION, in the generator: Anville Town's 419/420/421 stay houses. They fail the map
	-- test only because BW's town map types Anville as a landmark — the map types a place as a town when you
	-- can FLY there, and Anville is reached by train. It is a town, and its doors are houses.
	-- Curated buildings + the player's house/room override it (see transition_name).
