		-- Victory Road, Wellspring/Mistralton/Challenger's Caves, Twist Mountain, the Gear Station. No
		-- counter-example exists. A building's front door is type 3, the mat back out is type 1, and
		-- Castelia's street connectors are type 36 — never type 2. Inside the castle the four
		-- hall-to-hall links are type 2 on a 1x4 stair strip, the twelve side-room doors are type 3 1x1,
		-- and 277->278 is type 4 on a 3x1 archway: a different type AND a different shape from the four
		-- staircases in the same building, so the throne room is a ROOM off 277, not a floor above it.
		-- Room identities come from the game's own script text (a/0/0/3 banks 287-301, zone script bank =
		-- zonedata+0x0a), never from the ids; 265 and 273 are literally the same map (matrix 171) reused.
		-- ⚠ OURS, NOT THE GAME'S: the ROM has no floor strings at all (proven for Celestial Tower — every
