	--         Strength?". The cut tree's 10004 is the same shape with move 15 and message 0. So the two
	--         models are ONE obstacle with two graphics (a cave rock and an outdoor rock), which no amount
	--         of looking at their 15 zones could have settled.
	--         ⚠ The census that found them is research/re/boulder_census.py; the decode is
	--         research/re/common_script_dump.py. Its own header records the trap: the banked note said the
	--         10000+ scripts live in a/0/5/7 file 864, and 864 is the 7000..7799 range — decoding it gave a
	--         clean, plausible, entirely wrong disassembly. The categorize table is the only truth here.
	local HM_MODELS   = { [108]="Cut tree", [206]="Rock Smash rock",   -- 206 word per Ola + despawn model; native confirm queued
		[8195]="Strength boulder", [8197]="Strength boulder" }
	-- Functional NON-trainer NPCs named by their fixed SCRIPT, keyed on the live actor's SCRID (+0x14) —
