	-- STORY NPCs named BEFORE you talk (AUTO-GENERATED by research/re/gen_npc_vm.py; both ROMs identical). ⭐⭐⭐
	-- Uses a real SCRIPT INTERPRETER (research/re/script_vm.py). Talking to an NPC runs its own SCRID script
	-- (pokeplatinum field_control.c: ScriptManager_Set(.., MapObject_GetScript(object),..)); the VM EXECUTES
	-- that script — FOLLOWING CallRoutine(0x04) / Jump(0x1e) / If-When(0x20/1f) into sub-routines — and collects
	-- every message it can show (Message 0x3c / Message2 0x3d / Message3 0x48; msgId = u16 at op+4). So it reaches
	-- lines held in CALLED routines that a static scan can't see (Bianca's Mom, the Seven Sages, gym leaders...).
	-- The arg-byte table (how many bytes each opcode consumes — the thing that lets us step scripts without
	-- derailing) started from the community CheapScript B2W2 command table (BW1 shares the opcode set — verified
	-- 0x02 End / 0x04 CallRoutine / 0x28 SetVar / 0x2E LockAll(0 args) / 0x3D Message2 all match; op 0x74 =
	-- FacePlayer, NOT a message — that's why the earlier byte-scan of 0x74 invented a bogus "Bianca"). CheapScript
	-- had 144 of ~209 commands; research/re/bw_solve.py boundary-solved the rest (a length is right when it makes
	-- the NEXT word a valid opcode) -> all 209 known, 95% of scripts decode cleanly. NAME = the first message's
	-- speaker if prefixed, else the single distinct speaker; validated (<=3 words, all Capitalized).
	-- ⭐ KEYED BY THE LIVE ACTOR'S SCRID (+0x14), and the script it runs is slot **SCRID - 1**.
	-- ⛔⛔ SCRID IS 1-BASED, AND WE HAD IT 0-BASED UNTIL 2026-08-31 — every generated name sat one slot too
	-- low, game-wide. Ola heard it on Route 1: a plain Man (model 18, scrid 3) announced itself as "Cheren"
	-- while the real Cheren beside him (model 7, scrid 4) announced "Bianca".
	-- PROVEN IN WHITE'S OWN CODE, not carried over from Gen IV. FUN_02158cf0 = ScriptContext_LoadAndOffsetID
	-- (reached from FUN_02158c1c, the ScriptContext builder that loads the command table 0x0217064C via the
	-- literal at 0x02158CCC). It walks a 46-entry range table at 0x021701C8 ({lo, hi, a/0/5/7 file, unk,
	-- a/0/0/3 bank}, 10 bytes each: 2000+ common, 2100 heal nurse, 3000..4999 trainers — the already-banked
	-- SCRID-3000 — 7000+ items, 10110 shop) returning `scrid - lo`, and for anything below that falls through
	-- to `if (scrid != 0) { load THIS map's script file; return scrid - 1; }`. Its caller then does the
	-- JumpToOffsetID arithmetic we had already banked: ptr += offsetID*4 + table[offsetID].
	-- ⇒ **SCRID 0 IS THE NULL SCRIPT** (the else-branch loads a dummy), so a key of 0 can never name anyone;
	-- the four hand-added [0] entries were dead code and are gone.
	-- JumpToOffsetID still has NO bounds check, so a FLAG-SPAWNED actor's live scrid resolves to a slot even
	-- when its static a/1/2/5 scrid is out of range. Slots no live actor uses are harmless dead entries.
	-- ⚠ THE OLD "verified" CONFIRMED ITS OWN ASSUMPTION: research/re/npc_scrid_check.py opens
	-- "zone 317 (Route 1, known-good: Cheren=scrid3)" — the very actor that is a Man. And white.lua had
	-- already WRITTEN DOWN the contradiction (Lenora "scrid 2 while the battle sits in slot 1") and explained
	-- it away as "the talk scrid is not the battle slot". Two records of the bug, neither read as one.
	-- ⛔ AND THE SPRITE OUTRANKS THE SCRIPT (both at generation and live, see naming below). A cutscene slot
	-- opens on whoever speaks FIRST, which is often not the actor who owns it: Route 1's arrival scene belongs
	-- to Professor Juniper but opens on Cheren's line, and Nacrene Gym's slot belongs to Lenora but opens on
	-- Hawes bursting in. Ten sprites are exclusive to one character, so a name that contradicts the sprite is
	-- provably somebody else's line and is dropped — a generic word beats a wrong name.
	-- 214 names / 71 zones (+2 hand entries), White and Black identical. Regenerate with
	-- research/re/gen_npc_vm.py; the two hand entries below are the only ones it does not produce.
