	-- ── SAY THE TERRACE WHEN IT CHANGES (Ola, 2026-08-28) ────────────────────────────────────────────
	-- He originally asked for silence here (questions_victory_road.md Q1) and revised it once he had
	-- played it: "when you slide it should say what floor you end up on", and "when you're inside and
	-- walking outside again on a higher floor it still only says victory road and not the floor".
	-- Both are the same event -- ARRIVING ON A TERRACE -- so both come from this one latch. It is the
	-- Driftveil storey announcer's shape (ow.dv.step) for the same reason: the place changes without the
	-- zone changing, so the ordinary map-change announcer cannot see it.
	-- ⛔ NEVER CLEAR THE LATCH ON AN UNREADABLE FRAME, only on leaving the zone -- clearing it on a bad
	-- read re-announces the terrace you are already standing on, an unprompted interrupt saying nothing
	-- new (the exact defect codex-review caught in ow.dv.step on 2026-08-24).
	-- INTERRUPT vs QUEUE, by this project's standing rule: arriving in the zone, the PLACE NAME is the
	-- first thing on the new screen and interrupts, and the floor QUEUES behind it; a terrace change
	-- while already here IS the new screen, so it interrupts.
	-- ⚠ 1F IS SPOKEN ONLY ON A CHANGE, never as the first thing on entering the zone. Ola's no-1F rule
	-- ("1F shouldn't speak at all, so you don't know if the building has floors by coming from the
