	-- ⛔⛔ IS THIS ROCK BETWEEN STATES? One classifier, used by live(), fill() and sig(), because the last
	-- three rounds of this feature were all caused by two of them disagreeing.
	-- Two transitional phases, and the SECOND one is the trap: the horizontal push (action command 8..11,
	-- or origin disagreeing with current) and then the vertical FALL, which changes only world Y — so
	-- origin equals current, the command is reset, and the rock looks perfectly settled while it is still
	-- in the air. The engine raises status 0x280 at fall START and writes the save record only at the END,
	-- so "0x280 without a saved record" is exactly the airborne window.
	-- ⚠ This is the one that mattered most: without it sig() reported a CHANGED, non-nil layout during the
	-- fall, the follower re-planned into it, live() refused, and the Strength route was replaced by a
	-- generic one — on the FINAL push of every puzzle, the moment it must not happen (codex-review
	-- 2026-09-02, HIGH).
	function ow.st.busy(r)
		return r.moving or ((r.sta & 0x280) == 0x280 and r.saved ~= true)
	end
	-- ⭐ A FALLEN ROCK, BY THE ENGINE'S OWN PREDICATE — and it is the SAVE RECORD, nothing else. The game
	-- decides whether a class-0x1D tile is still solid in player-collision helper White 0x021A5284, which
	-- reaches 0x0216E53C: map the actor to its slot, read `manager[+0x2C] + slot*12`, and ask 0x0216E4B0
	-- whether that record is written. No status bit is consulted anywhere on that path.
	-- ⚠ I had `(sta & 0x280) == 0x280 and saved`. The status half is set at fall START and is right while
	-- the rock is on screen, but it is a LIVE-ACTOR mark: nothing promises it survives leaving the area and
	-- coming back, which is exactly the "the tool may not realise the hole is filled" limitation I wrote
	-- down rather than fixed. The record does survive — it is in the save file — and it carries the
	-- POSITION, so ow.st.fill no longer needs the actor to be loaded at all. The airborne window is still
	-- excluded, by ow.st.busy, which is where that belongs.
	function ow.st.down(r) return r.saved == true end
	-- The tiles that are floor because a rock fell into them. Used by pf_chunks so that the WHOLE router -
	-- A*, the reachability flood, the follower's route-ahead check - crosses a filled hole, not just this
	-- module's private search. Without it the tool guides the player to fill the hole and then refuses to
	-- walk over it, which is the most baffling possible moment to fail (codex-review 2026-09-02).
	-- ⚠ Only a LANDED rock fills a hole — ow.st.down requires the saved record, so a rock still falling
	-- does not open the bridge early. That matters: it is the difference between "you may walk here now"
	-- and "you may walk here in twenty frames".
