	-- positions flips immediately - firing a re-plan mid-push, at the one moment live() refuses to read
	-- the room, so pf_build would fall back to a plain best-effort route WITHOUT a `stk` and the tool
	-- would stop watching for pushes altogether (codex-review verification 2026-09-02).
	-- Returning nil while anything moves makes the follower hold: its re-plan block does nothing on nil,
	-- the route stands, and one settled change arrives when the push completes. That is exactly the
	-- "freeze and re-read on a transitional state" the RE report asked for.
	-- ⚠ AND IT GOES THROUGH live(), NOT raw(). It used to apply its own busy test to raw()'s output, which
	-- made it a THIRD classifier beside live() and the old fill() — and it disagreed: in the state where a
	-- saved record and the loaded actor contradict each other, live() refuses to read the room while sig()
	-- happily published a stable fingerprint of it (codex-review 2026-09-02, part of the HIGH). One read,
	-- one classifier, for the third and last time in this module.
	-- ⚠ `tl` IS THE CALLER'S TILE VIEW AND IT IS NOT OPTIONAL IN PRACTICE. Without it live() cannot apply
	-- the push/fall handoff test, so sig() would publish a changed layout for a rock that is standing in
	-- its hole and about to drop — one re-plan, answered with a generic route, and "a later correction does
	-- not retract the already-spoken instruction" (codex verification 2026-09-02). Both call sites have a
