	-- `blocked` = tile keys nothing may move onto (other boulders, hard actors).
	-- ⛔⛔ `filled` = the holes a rock has already landed in. They must be handed in separately, because
	-- the `tl` every caller passes is pf_tile, and pf_tile deliberately reports a filled hole as ordinary
	-- FLOOR so the player can walk over it (cs.stfill). That is the right view for the PLAYER and the wrong
	-- one for a BOULDER: natively the tile is still class 0x1D, so a second rock pushed onto it would fall
	-- in, not roll across. Two different questions about the same tile; collapsing them into one reader is
