		end
		-- ⛔⛔ AIM AT THE ACCEPTED TILE THAT IS ACTUALLY REACHABLE — not at the doorway, and not at one
		-- chosen tile beside it. Both of those have now failed in the same building, for opposite reasons:
		--   • Aiming at the DOORWAY relies on A* stopping at the Manhattan-nearest reachable tile, which
		--     since we learned the engine's approach rule can be a tile on a side the door does not open
		--     from at all. That is what left Ola below the 5F stairwell.
		--   • Aiming at ONE tile of the correct side is what the old comment here warned about, and I
		--     reintroduced it: "if that one tile is walled off from the player, A* stops somewhere useless
		--     even when another edge of the same doorway is reachable". Ola, immediately: "it says can't
		--     reach from here... most doors only have 1 way to get near them, the closest tile is usually
		--     always the right one, not here."
		-- So do neither. Flood-fill from the player once and take the accepted tile with the shortest REAL
		-- path — the side comes from the engine's rule, the choice within that side comes from the map.
		-- One fill per plan, never per frame, and only for a warp that names a side.
		if ow.at_reg(e.reg, sx, sz) then say("You're there", true); pf = nil; return end
		if e.reg and e.reg[5] then
