			-- ⛔⛔ AND A STRENGTH ROOM IS THE SAME CASE AS THE GYM BELOW — Ola, 2026-09-02, in Mistralton
			-- Cave: "I tried to go to the second transition here, which is the next room, but it said can't
			-- reach, but it should just guide me through the puzzle." His dump shows the transition was
			-- correctly LISTED and gated ("warp 1 -> zone 334 ... KEPT, gated: Strength"), so the nav side
			-- was right; the route died here, one call before ow.st was ever asked. reg_aim floods on FOOT,
			-- the doorway is behind a hole a boulder has to fill, so it answers "none" and this refused the
			-- whole route — the identical shape to the Opelucid bug documented immediately below, which is
			-- why that exemption existed at all. It was hardcoded to that one room; the codex review
			-- flagged the gap for Strength zones and I deferred it, and this is exactly what it cost.
			-- ⚠ THE PREDICATE IS "THIS ROOM HAS A LEG PLANNER THAT CAN OPEN THE WAY", not "this room is
			-- special". Keep the entry's own aim and let pf_build decide; the door's approach side is still
			-- enforced on the final approach, when he is near it and reg_aim can answer.
			-- ⚠ AND THE STRENGTH EXEMPTION IS EARNED PER DOOR, NOT GRANTED PER ZONE (codex-review
			-- 2026-09-02). Waiving the refusal for every boulder zone meant a door that genuinely cannot be
