			-- enforced on the final approach, when he is actually near it and reg_aim can answer.
		end
		-- ⭐ CATCH A GOAL THAT IS NOT WHERE ITS OWNER IS, AT THE MOMENT THE ROUTE IS BORN.
		-- Ola, 2026-08-26: routed to Brycen, told "arrived", and found him a tile up and to the LEFT — a
		-- diagonal, which is not a tile you can talk to anyone from. I proved what it is NOT: nothing
		-- authored in zone 114 sits at the tile we aimed at (every furniture, actor, sign and event record
		-- checked in research/re/z114_brycen.py), both NPC readers take the actor's live tile from
		-- +0x3C/+0x40, and ow.replan reuses pf.gx/gz rather than drifting them. What I could NOT prove is
		-- where the wrong tile came from, because by the time he dumped, the route was long since built.
