May poison targets when a Pokémon makes contact.|Restores a little HP when withdrawn from battle.|Protects the Pokémon from Defense-lowering attacks.|Boosts the Pokémon's Speed in a sandstorm.|Makes status-changing moves more likely to miss.|Boosts move power when the Pokémon moves last.|Comes out disguised as the Pokémon in back.|It transforms itself into the Pokémon it is facing.|Passes through the foe's barrier and strikes.|Contact with this Pokémon spreads this Ability.|Boosts Attack after knocking out any Pokémon.|Raises Attack when hit by a Dark-type move.|Some move types scare it and boost its Speed.|Reflects status- changing moves.|Boosts Attack when hit by a Grass-type move.|Gives priority to a status move.|Boosts certain moves' power in a sandstorm.|Inflicts damage to the Pokémon on contact.|Changes the Pokémon's shape when HP is halved.|Boosts the accuracy of its allies and itself.|Moves can be used regardless of Abilities.|Moves can be used regardless of Abilities."

		-- a/0/1/6 file 668 = species -> UNOVA dex number (156 present of 650). An absent species has 999 there
		-- and the screen prints no number at all, so this reader omits the field entirely rather than saying a
		-- number the player cannot see. The NARC id is a runtime global, so the FILE was found by CONTENT, not
